---
// Airogine's privacy policy for this website. It describes what the site
// actually does - keep it in step: no cookies, cookieless Vercel Web Analytics
// (served from this site), no third-party requests (fonts are self-hosted), the
// demo form, and the host's logs. If any of that changes, change this page in
// the same commit. Needs legal review.
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import LegalContact from '../components/LegalContact.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Airogine collects through this website, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept, and the choices and rights you have."
  updated={site.legal.privacyUpdated}
>
  <p class="legal-intro">
    This policy explains how Airogine ("we", "us") handles personal information collected through this website. In
    short: the site has no cookies or advertising, it counts visits without identifying you, and the only personal
    information we ask for is what you choose to put in the demo request form.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scope">What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>
    It covers this website and the documentation on it. It does not cover the Nexus software. Nexus runs on your own
    servers, and the data it collects from your plant (tag values, alarms, history, users and their activity) stays there:
    Airogine does not receive it. The only things Nexus sends to Airogine are covered under
    <a href="#nexus">Nexus licensing</a> below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <h3>What you give us</h3>
  <p>When you book a demo, the form asks for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, work email address and company;</li>
    <li>your role;</li>
    <li>optionally, the protocols on your site and a description of your device list.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please don't put anything in the device list that you aren't comfortable sharing with us, such as passwords, network
    addresses or other security details of your plant. If you write to us, we receive what you send.
  </p>

  <h3>What is collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Like any website, the servers that deliver these pages receive technical information with each request: your IP
    address, browser and device type, the page asked for, the referring page and the time. Our hosting provider records
    it in short-lived logs that are used to deliver the site, keep it secure and fix problems. We don't use it to build
    profiles of visitors.
  </p>

  <h3>Visit statistics</h3>
  <p>
    To see which pages are read and where visitors come from, we use Vercel Web Analytics, provided by our hosting
    provider. For each page view it records the page, the referring page, your browser, operating system and device
    type, and your country, worked out from your IP address. It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser. To
    count visitors without identifying them, it uses a value calculated from your request that is discarded after 24
    hours. Your IP address is not stored. We only see the results as totals, such as page views and visitors per page.
  </p>

  <h3>What we don't do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The site sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and stores nothing in your browser.</li>
    <li>
      There is <strong>no advertising and no social media tracking</strong>, and no tracking pixels. The visit statistics
      can't follow you from one day to the next, or across other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pages load nothing from other companies' servers: fonts, images, the documentation search and the visit statistics
      script are served from this site.
    </li>
    <li>We don't sell personal information, and we don't share it for targeted advertising.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To arrange and prepare your demo, and to answer your questions about Nexus.</li>
    <li>To follow up about the demo and about Nexus afterwards. You can ask us to stop at any time.</li>
    <li>To deliver the website, keep it secure and working, and prevent abuse.</li>
    <li>To see which pages are useful and where visitors come from, so we can improve the site.</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations, and to establish or defend legal claims.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For visitors in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom: we handle demo requests because you asked us to
    take steps towards a possible contract with you, or for our legitimate interest in answering enquiries about our
    product. We handle the technical information and visit statistics above for our legitimate interest in running a secure
    website and improving it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> that run things for us under contract and only on our instructions: the hosting
      provider that serves this site and provides its visit statistics (Vercel), the service that delivers demo requests to us by email (Resend), and the
      services we use to send email and keep track of our conversations with customers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>An integrator or distributor</strong> that resells Nexus in your region, if you ask us to put you in touch,
      or agree to it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authorities</strong>, where the law requires it, or where it is needed to protect the rights, safety or
      property of Airogine, our customers or others.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A buyer or successor</strong>, if Airogine is involved in a merger, acquisition or sale of its business, in
      which case this policy continues to apply to the information transferred.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="nexus">Nexus licensing</h2>
  <p>
    If you use Nexus and activate a license online, the gateway sends Airogine's license server the activation key, the
    gateway's install ID and name, and the Nexus version. Once a day it then asks for renewals, sending the install ID,
    the current license's ID and the version. We use these to issue and renew licenses. An activation request you send
    us by email carries the same install ID and gateway name. No plant data is ever sent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Demo requests and correspondence:</strong> while we are in contact with you about Nexus, and then for up to
      two years after our last contact, unless you become a customer, in which case we keep what we need to manage the
      relationship. You can ask us to delete it sooner.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> for the short period our hosting provider keeps them.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visit statistics:</strong> the value used to count visitors is discarded after 24 hours. The totals,
      which identify no one, are kept for as long as our hosting plan provides.
    </li>
    <li>We keep information for longer only where the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served only over HTTPS. Access to the information you send us is limited to the people who need it to
    answer you, and our service providers are chosen for their security practices. No system is perfectly secure, so we
    can't guarantee that information will never be accessed without permission, but if something happens that affects
    your information, we'll tell you as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2 id="transfers">Where it is handled</h2>
  <p>
    Airogine is based in the United States, and our service providers may handle information in the United States and
    other countries. Where we transfer personal information out of the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we
    rely on safeguards the law recognizes, such as the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>Wherever you are, you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what personal information we hold about you, and give you a copy;</li>
    <li>correct it;</li>
    <li>delete it;</li>
    <li>stop contacting you about Nexus.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, the law may give you further rights. Residents of US states with privacy laws, such as
    California, may also ask what categories of information we collect and disclose, and have an authorized agent make
    a request for them. Visitors in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom may also object to how we use their
    information or ask us to restrict it, ask for it in a portable format, and complain to their data protection
    authority. We'll never treat you differently for using these rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, contact us at <LegalContact />. We'll confirm your request, may need to check that it is
    yours, and answer within the time the law allows.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because the visit statistics don't identify you or follow you across websites, there is nothing to opt out of with
    Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signals, and we don't sell or share personal information in any case. If you
    would rather not be counted at all, most content blockers stop the statistics script.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site and Nexus are for businesses. They are not meant for children, and we don't knowingly collect personal
    information from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to a few other websites, such as protocol and standards pages. Their own privacy policies apply when
    you visit them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle personal information, we'll update this page and the date at the top. If a change is
    significant, we'll make it clear on the site and, where we have your email address and the change affects you, tell
    you before it applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your information go to Airogine at <LegalContact />. See also our
    <a href={url('/terms/')}>terms of use</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
